---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The round that exists because the starting constraint turned out to be
// wrong. The slide carries the reframing; the merge mechanics and the
// CRDT comparison get said out loud, with the bench open if asked.
---

<Slide subtitle="Two people, one item">
	<div class="grid gap-13">
		<div class="text-strong max-w-[1500px] text-5xl">
			&ldquo;One editor at a time&rdquo; was the starting constraint, not the
			destination.
		</div>
		<div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-7">
			<div>
				<div class="text-subdued text-xs font-medium uppercase">Today</div>
				<div class="text-subdued mt-3 text-2xl">
					Several people can edit. Nobody sees anything until reload. Last write wins.
				</div>
			</div>
			<div>
				<div class="text-subdued text-xs font-medium uppercase">So a lock is</div>
				<div class="text-subdued mt-3 text-2xl">
					Not a design. Scaffolding, and a habit that has to be untrained later.
				</div>
			</div>
			<div>
				<div class="text-subdued text-xs font-medium uppercase">Instead</div>
				<div class="text-subdued mt-3 text-2xl">
					Merge what they started from, what they typed, and what is stored now.
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="text-subdued text-3xl">
			Both changed the same words, so it garbles.
			<span class="text-strong">
				Tidying a sentence beats reconstructing a paragraph you cannot see.
			</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</Slide>
